 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the pathogenic fungus Verticillium dahliae and its interactions with various organisms and chemicals. The fungus causes disease in cotton and regulates the development of the VdMFS2 gene. VdMFS2 is expressed in cotton and is a host for the fungus Vd592. The fungus has several proteins, including AAs, G2WZT4, and SCRPs. The ΔVdMFS2 mutants have altered protein secretion compared to the wild-type fungus. The cluster also includes various methods and tools used to study the fungus, such as HIGS, pTRV2-00, and Student’s t-test.",
